      "side": 1,
      "message": "The return value of `ECDSA_SIG_set0` doesn\u0027t have any meaning beyond success/failure:\n\n```\n// ECDSA_SIG_set0 sets |sig|\u0027s components to |r| and |s|, neither of which may\n// be NULL. On success, it takes ownership of each argument and returns one.\n// Otherwise, it returns zero.\n```\n\nThe implementation of ECDSA_SIG_set0 does not push any errors to the queue:\n\n```\nint ECDSA_SIG_set0(ECDSA_SIG *sig, BIGNUM *r, BIGNUM *s) {\n  if (r \u003d\u003d NULL || s \u003d\u003d NULL) {\n    return 0;\n  }\n  BN_free(sig-\u003er);\n  BN_free(sig-\u003es);\n  sig-\u003er \u003d r;\n  sig-\u003es \u003d s;\n  return 1;\n}\n```\n\nSo IMO trying to report the error number is not worth it.",
